                    insight_transformation: `Transformation earned: you lifted digital share to the board target, moved conversion toward the 2.6% benchmark via the replatform, held the 71% awareness that subsidises CAC, and funded attribution so the return is provable. Every number connects to a decision — the defense the board trusts.`,
                    insight_brandcut:       `Over-cut brand: you slashed TV and catalog to chase the digital number, awareness slid below the danger line, and blended CAC climbed because you are now buying customers the brand used to deliver for free. The delayed penalty Mazurek warns of arrived at the year-end board — demand capture cannibalised demand generation.`,
                    insight_spreadthin:     `Spread thin: you funded breadth across the martech envelope and starved the one investment with the most leverage. The replatform stalled at partial funding and conversion barely moved. Sequencing — foundational before nice-to-have — is the discipline you skipped.`,
                    insight_noattribution:  `Skipped attribution: conversion may have improved, but you cannot say which channels drove the new revenue. Next year’s 64 mln zł has nowhere to point, and you cannot prove causality at the board. Measurement capability is what protects marketing’s seat at the table.`,
                    insight_cacchasing:     `Optimised CAC in isolation: you drove acquisition cost down by chasing discount-seekers whose order value is low and who never return. You won the acquisition metric and lost the unit economics — acquisition cost is meaningless without lifetime value beside it.`,
                    insight_ceded:          `Ceded control: you treated the pivot as an IT or agency project and the board’s question writes itself — if marketing does not own the customer outcome, why does the company need a CMO? Mazurek’s core point: transformation is marketing-led, not technology-led.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed pivot: parts of the strategy worked, but the reallocation, martech sequencing and measurement did not fully reinforce each other — enough seams that the board can still question whether the return is real and repeatable.`,
                    insight_checkpoint:     `You missed the 30 September checkpoint (below 16% digital share), the trigger the board set for the 20% budget cut and the agency takeover. Even a strong year-end cannot fully undo losing strategic control at the half-year.`,
                    insight_brandlow:       `Brand awareness fell below a safe floor: the crown-jewel asset that made your acquisition cheap eroded, and blended CAC carries a permanent tax until you rebuild it. Awareness is a CAC subsidy you spent.`,
                    insight_targetmiss:     `Digital share finished short of the 20% board target: the reallocation and martech did not generate the demand-capture and conversion lift needed within the frozen envelope.`,
                    insight_convlow:        `Conversion never reached the benchmark: you hit the share number on spend and demand capture rather than the conversion foundation, leaving the most durable lever — the replatform — under-realised.`,

                    hint_checkpoint:        `You are below the 16% half-year checkpoint — the board’s trigger for the cut and agency takeover. Move decisively into high-intent demand capture and fund the conversion replatform next round before control slips.`,
                    hint_brand:             `Brand awareness has fallen into the danger zone — and a low awareness is now a permanent tax on blended CAC. Restore a brand floor before the erosion compounds further.`,
                    hint_brandpending:      `You cut brand hard — a delayed awareness penalty is queued and will hit the year-end scorecard, dragging CAC up with it. Rebuild a brand floor now to soften the landing.`,
                    hint_attribution:       `You have built capability but skipped attribution — you will not be able to prove which channels drove revenue at the board. Fund the attribution layer so the ROI defense holds.`,
                    hint_cacchasing:        `Your low CAC is built on discount-seekers with poor order value and no repeat — manage unit economics (order value, retention) alongside CAC before the board exposes the hollow win.`,
                    hint_spreadthin:        `You spread the envelope thin and starved the leverage play — the replatform stalled. Concentrate funding on the highest-leverage build rather than a little of everything.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — share at target, brand held, ROI provable through attribution. Close it out: a causal defense and managing unit economics alongside CAC will hold it before the board.`,

